From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:03:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/48] net: xpon: omci: release the T-CONT when the OLT
 unassigns its Alloc-ID

G.988 (T-CONT, Alloc-ID) gives the attribute an unusable value until the
OLT assigns an Alloc-ID: 0x00FF or 0xFFFF in G-PON. Writing one of those
back is how the OLT takes the T-CONT away.

The agent passed any written value to the provider as a valid binding.
With 0xFFFF the Airoha backend refused it (Alloc-IDs are 12 bits) and
the Set failed with "processing error"; with 0x00FF it bound a hardware
channel to Alloc-ID 255. Unbind the T-CONT for both values, and do not
stage services on a T-CONT that holds either of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index c5b3262..025dc95 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -2696,6 +2696,15 @@ static int omci_agent_mib_reset_locked(struct omci_device *odev, bool all,
 	return ret ?: reset_ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * G.988 T-CONT Alloc-ID: before the OLT assigns one, and when it takes it
+ * back, the attribute holds an unusable value, 0x00FF or 0xFFFF in G-PON.
+ */
+static bool omci_tcont_alloc_unassigned(u16 alloc_id)
+{
+	return alloc_id == 0x00ff || alloc_id == 0xffff;
+}
+
 static int omci_agent_hw_update(struct omci_device *odev,
 				struct omci_mib_object *object,
 				u8 action, const u8 *content)
@@ -2718,10 +2727,11 @@ static int omci_agent_hw_update(struct omci_device *odev,
 	case OMCI_CLASS_TCONT:
 		if (!ops->set_tcont)
 			return 0;
-		if (action == OMCI_MSG_TYPE_DELETE)
+		value = get_unaligned_be16(object->data);
+		if (action == OMCI_MSG_TYPE_DELETE ||
+		    omci_tcont_alloc_unassigned(value))
 			return ops->set_tcont(odev, object->entity_id, 0xffff,
 					      false);
-		value = get_unaligned_be16(object->data);
 		return ops->set_tcont(odev, object->entity_id, value, true);
 	case OMCI_CLASS_GEM_PORT_CTP:
 		if (!ops->set_gem_port)
@@ -3003,7 +3013,8 @@ omci_agent_stage_service_rule_locked(struct omci_device *odev,
 	service.tcont_entity_id = get_unaligned_be16(gem->data + 2);
 	tcont = omci_mib_lookup(agent, OMCI_CLASS_TCONT,
 				 service.tcont_entity_id);
-	if (!tcont || get_unaligned_be16(tcont->data) == 0xffff)
+	if (!tcont ||
+	    omci_tcont_alloc_unassigned(get_unaligned_be16(tcont->data)))
 		return -ENOENT;
 	/* Carry the Alloc-ID: the backend may need it to rebuild the channel. */
 	service.alloc_id = get_unaligned_be16(tcont->data);
